Rule 10 (at least one of the tensors should have elements or be scalar)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= ndim(x) = 0 ∨ ndim(y) = 0 ∨ (ndim(x) > 0 ∨ ndim(y) > 0)
>>
Rule 11 (If x is scalar, y must be valid type)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 then (dtype_(y) = 7 ∨ dtype_(y) = 8 ∨ dtype_(y) = 3 ∨ dtype_(y) = 6 ∨ dtype_(y) = 2 ∨ dtype_(y) = 1 ∨ dtype_(y) = 4)
>>
Rule 14 (If x is scalar, y must be a valid type, or vice versa)
